WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.120
Speaker 1: Welcome back to the David Pakman&nbsp;
Show. I'm producer Pat Forde, filling in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:07.760
for David today as he continues his paternity&nbsp;
leave. We're now finding out more having to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:12.240
with you of all the shooting that took place a few&nbsp;
weeks ago and specifically the police department's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.800
failed response to it. We're now finding out that&nbsp;
they're working with a private law firm to prevent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.600
the release of details to the public as to what&nbsp;
exactly they were doing as a gunman was inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:27.280
Rob Elementary School murdering 19 children and&nbsp;
two teachers. We already knew that their story had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:34.080
changed a bunch, and we knew that they hesitated.&nbsp;
There was a dispute over when exactly they arrived&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.160
and whether they confronted the shooter at the&nbsp;
door, whether that door was propped open by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:43.600
a teacher. But at the very least, it was clear&nbsp;
from early on that they didn't follow protocol,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:48.400
that they waited and waited, and they didn't want&nbsp;
to go into the school out of fear for their own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:53.040
lives, and that they even went so far as to hold&nbsp;
back parents who were trying to go in and save&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.720
their kids, knowing that the cops weren't&nbsp;
going to do anything for them. In addition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:01.440
we found out this week that cops were in the&nbsp;
hallway of the school but refused to advance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:05.120
even though they certainly had the proper&nbsp;
equipment, the rifles and the guards and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.680
the shields and everything that you would need to&nbsp;
confront the shooter. And they were also spending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.880
spending a bunch of time trying to find a key&nbsp;
to the classroom that the shooter was hiding in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.920
even though the door was unlocked the entire&nbsp;
time. So they didn't need a key. So now the police&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.880
department wants to make sure nothing more gets&nbsp;
out. The public records they're trying to hide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:31.280
which include the body camera footage, the&nbsp;
photos, 911 calls, emails, text messages.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:35.920
They're trying to hide all of it. A letter from&nbsp;
the city to Texas Attorney General Ken Paxton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:40.320
says that the department doesn't want to release&nbsp;
the information because for one, it's being sued,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.440
which is somewhat understandable, I guess, but&nbsp;
also because it includes highly embarrassing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:52.160
information and that the info is not of legitimate&nbsp;
concern to the public. So how brazen can they be?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:56.960
They're out now admitting that what's in the&nbsp;
documents is embarrassing, meaning that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:02.400
did wrong, that they knew that they did wrong,&nbsp;
and that it's just not important, apparently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:06.000
for the public to learn about, even though this&nbsp;
is a matter having to do with the deaths of 21&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.480
people in the community, many of them little&nbsp;
kids. And you're going to say that it's of no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.640
concern to the public. How can you get away with&nbsp;
saying something like that? The city and its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:19.600
police department argue it should be exempted&nbsp;
from releasing police officer training guides,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:25.680
police policy and procedure manuals, shift change&nbsp;
schedules, security details and blueprints of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:30.960
secured facilities. Because these could be used&nbsp;
to decipher methods, techniques and strategies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:36.720
for preventing and predicting crime. Well, okay,&nbsp;
to some degree I understand this one. But clearly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.600
whatever methods, techniques and strategies they&nbsp;
had ahead of this mass shooting, they either&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:46.560
didn't work or they didn't follow them. They chose&nbsp;
not to use them. And so it would be nice to review&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:51.360
the process and see how we could go about changing&nbsp;
it. So this is going to be a travesty if they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:55.360
allowed to block the documents from public view,&nbsp;
especially because they've already been caught&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.520
in so many lies. And the public has a right to&nbsp;
know about this stuff, right? Because it's their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:05.360
tax dollars that were being spent and it was their&nbsp;
community that was ultimately hurt by all of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.360
and hurt by their failed response. And this&nbsp;
is a situation that probably should lead to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.520
some criminal charges. I'm not saying that you&nbsp;
should charge the entire police department,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:18.320
but certainly the officers who were there who&nbsp;
had the opportunity to go in and decided not to.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:21.920
Many of them should be charged with child neglect.&nbsp;
That's what happened to that officer in Parkland&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.920
who refused to go into the school. That should&nbsp;
probably happen to many of the officers who were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:31.120
on scene there. And at the very least, many of&nbsp;
those cops should be losing their jobs because not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:35.840
only did those who followed the police officers&nbsp;
fail, those 21 victims and their families,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:41.680
not only did they fail to involve the community,&nbsp;
they also failed society at large, like the public&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:47.120
needs to be able to trust that if it hits the&nbsp;
fan, the cops are going to be there around the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:52.560
corner to protect them. That's why police officers&nbsp;
get the respect and the reverence that they do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:56.720
among most people in the country because they're&nbsp;
believed to be putting their lives on the line.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:01.200
You can't have a situation where the community&nbsp;
views cops is just the people who are out there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:06.960
giving traffic tickets or breaking up high school&nbsp;
parties, acting like tough guys in so doing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:11.200
but then not step in when a situation&nbsp;
like this really calls for it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:15.680
really calls for police attention. So let's&nbsp;
cross our fingers and hope that this effort&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:19.920
to block the body cam footage and the text&nbsp;
and all the other relevant information isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:24.240
successful because the public deserves to know&nbsp;
about this. Right. And these cops need to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:29.040
held accountable for their dereliction of&nbsp;
duty, not just in response to the specific&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:33.760
shooting and the 21 victims, but also for the&nbsp;
ramifications that it has for society at large.

